# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cottage Surgical (cottagedme) — environment variables
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values.
# `.env.local` is gitignored — never commit real credentials.
#
# Keys starting with NEXT_PUBLIC_ are bundled into the browser, so only put
# intentionally public values there (the Supabase anon key is protected by
# RLS). Keys without the prefix are server-side only and must never reach the
# browser.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase (client-side) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# From: Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Supabase (migrations only — NOT exposed to Next.js clients) ───────
# Full Postgres connection string used by scripts/run_migrations.py.
# Dashboard > Project Settings > Database > Connection string > URI (session pooler).
# Substitute [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the database password.
DB_CONNECTION=

# ── App public URL (server-side; powers auth redirects / invite links) ─
# Add ${APP_PUBLIC_URL}/set-password to Supabase > Auth > URL Configuration
# > Redirect URLs when that flow is enabled.
APP_PUBLIC_URL=

# ── Feature flags (client-side) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Internal tool: public self-serve signup stays OFF; users are invited by an
# admin. Leave UNSET to keep signup hidden; set true only if ever needed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SELF_SERVE_SIGNUP=
